      "message": "For one to many:\n* \"joined eager loading only makes sense when the size of the collections are relatively small.\"\n* where as, \"subquery load makes sense when the collections are larger.\"\nhttp://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/orm/loading_relationships.html\n\nThe user collections (local_user, password...) would be small; thus joined loading would perform better here. My only reservation is, that when I was researching hybrid properties, I remember reading that subquery loading prevented some errors. I\u0027m not finding those articles now, however this may be why you are failing some tempest tests such as:\ntempest.api.identity.admin.v2.test_users.UsersTestJSON.test_update_user_password\n\nThe hybrid properties may need to be tweaked if we go with joined loading.",
